Rāma keeps first night outside settled land wakeful --- Pities sleepless Daśaratha and sated Kaikēyī --- Fears Kaikēyī will cast off aged helpless king --- Calls desire weightier than wealth and dharma --- Pities lone Bharata enjoying Kōsala as king --- Fears proud Kaikēyī will torment Kausalyā Sumitrā --- Bids LakṣmaṆa guard helpless Kausalyā while he goes lone --- Reproaches himself for leaving long-cherished mother --- LakṣmaṆa says none live severed like fish from water --- Rāma resolves firm forest dwelling in dharma
